# Memory management
# Some code was borrowed from Phil Opp's Blog (http://os.phil-opp.com/allocating-frames.html)
#
# EXPERIMENT NOTE: Deor (see /specification) has no unsafe, no atomics, no raw
# pointers, no bitwise ops, no traits/generics, and no static mut globals.
# This file is a physical-frame allocator built entirely out of those things.
# So almost every declaration below is a thin Deor-shaped `fn`/`struct`/`enum`
# skin wrapped around a `raw` opaque type and a `rust` block that carries the
# real logic verbatim. That split is the honest answer to "what would this
# look like in Deor" -- the skin is Deor, the guts stay Rust.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Opaque handles onto types this file doesn't own (rmm crate, sibling modules)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

